      "notes": "Real time, one continuous uncut take, 30 fps, 780x1688 (390x844 at 2x). Shop generated by gemini-3.5-flash-lite (no fallback: read from the production log), photos by the image model. Build: 'submitted' -> hunting animation -> 'found-shop' (= 'build-first-paint': the hunting screen names the shop, 2.2 s) -> 'shop-open' (grid with first products, 2.5 s) -> photos fade in -> 'shop-visible' (all 10 products in, every photo on screen loaded, 8.8 s). The grid is left alone while it fills, then read slowly ('scroll-start'..'scroll-end'). Pay: the sheet opens on the simulated wallet while Stripe probes; the real Stripe test-mode wallet button (Apple Pay, 'TEST PAYMENT · YOUR CARD IS NOT CHARGED') is fully painted at 'wallet-visible' and held ~2 s; never pressed: 'simulated-pay-link' taps 'Or use the simulated pay', then double-click, scan, processing, tick. The simulated sheet shows the app's own 'S-Pankki Debit •••• 4821 · Invented demo card'."
